Z||000000||Jake_Dragon||02-05-2001||09:04 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> <BR>Well it seems everything I touch on this car needs replaced, well I guess if I keep going I will have a new car or at least a new drive train. After fixing the plugged exhaust the car would start and run but as soon as I put it in gear it stalls. when I try to start the car sounds like it is out of time. I purchased a new cap and roter and when I removed the old one everything was covered with rust (Thick) I can replace the ignition mod and pickup coil for $40 but every thing is still full of rust, for $100 I can get a new distributor. What do you think? clean what I have or replace it and not take the chance of breaking somthing when I clean it. <P>------------------<BR>Glenn Leber||||reg||5
Z||000001||DavidHenshaw||02-05-2001||09:21 PM||||Jake, if you want to know that the car will go you will want to replace the distributor. Mine would run and not run intermittantly. It wasn't the cap, rotor, plug wires, ignition module, or the coil; you guessed it, it was a rusty distributor. Its been 4,000 miles since replacement and there have been NO problems.<P>Dave<P>86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||Alex4mula||02-06-2001||04:03 PM||||Hay Jake;<P>Where you can get that distributor for $100? I would be interested. I remove and clean mine like once a year to keep the rust from growing but still doesn't look too pretty. The car seems to run fine but I wonder if I would gain some HP back with a new one.||||reg||1
Z||000003||CHARLIE FERGUSON||02-06-2001||04:10 PM||||replace that distributor! you'll be glad you did, also if your budget allows replace the coil, preferably a hi-pro like accel. i did both and my car run 10 times better.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Jake_Dragon||02-06-2001||04:22 PM||||AutoZone <BR>1535 N. Florida ave.<BR>Lakeland, Fl.<BR>863 682 8904<BR>There is a $50 core so bring your old one.<BR>I am on my way to pick one up now. Coil will have to wait till I hit the lottery or next check.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>||||reg||10
